  "caption": "Gifford et al. 2014 Lab Chip 14, 4496\u20134505, Fig. 6 (the micrograph; scale from the printed 125 \u00b5m centre, 4.5248 \u00b5m/px; the rows at 49.81\u00b0 on the image) with the first rc6 Fig. 6 variant (uniform legs 588 um apart), all four legs on ONE map, fitted on the ends of legs 5, 3 and 1 (cyan: the claim, legs 5, 3 and 1 with their divider walls and their turns as far as the frame shows them, leg 7 to 6 rows before its drawn end; amber: the outlet stretch and leg 7's end).  Registration: scale and rotation from the printed centre width and the rows on the image, rotation measured on the image; translation fitted on features and, independently, by chamfer matching (they agree within 0.0 / 0.2 px along / across).  Nearest-outline offset: median 1.76 \u00b5m, 90th percentile 6.77 \u00b5m (n 17525); for comparison 6.18 \u00b5m with the mask shifted half a pitch along and 2.57 \u00b5m with it shifted 5 \u00b5m across.  This mask's legs 2, 4, 6 lie where the generator's uniform paperclip puts them (588 \u00b5m apart), not where the image's turns put them, so the turns test that layout: the image's 16 turn walls lie a median 23.6 \u00b5m (90th percentile 59.7, max 230) from the mask's nearest edge, and the mask's own turn centre lies -1454 \u00b5m across from the image's: the turns are not concentric with the image's (a radius comparison about one centre does not apply).  Leg 7, not in the fit, lies -0.26 \u00b5m across from where its own end registers it.",
